body:
Mistakes I have made (and seen):

- Using `(lo + hi) / 2` in languages with fixed-size integers. Use `lo + (hi - lo) / 2`.
- Mixing `lo <= hi` and `lo < hi` loops with the wrong update rule.
- Forgetting that binary search also works on the **answer**, not only on arrays.

```cpp
int lo = 0, hi = n - 1, ans = -1;
while (lo <= hi) {
    int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
    if (ok(mid)) { ans = mid; hi = mid - 1; }
    else lo = mid + 1;
}
```
